<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Docker on GUI Free Life</title><link>http://guifreelife.com/tags/docker/</link><description>Recent content in Docker on GUI Free Life</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 09 Aug 2017 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://guifreelife.com/tags/docker/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>How to push an image to an unexposed OpenShift Docker registry</title><link>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2017/08/09/Pushing-To-OpenShift-Registry/</link><pubDate>Wed, 09 Aug 2017 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2017/08/09/Pushing-To-OpenShift-Registry/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;How do I push an image to the OpenShift Docker registry if it is not exposed outside the cluster?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Login to a member node&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Get on a machine that has docker and participates in the cluster SDN or can somehow access that network. (eg. &lt;code&gt;172.30.0.0/16&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get the IP of the registry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#eed;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;oc get svc docker-registry -n default --template &lt;span style="color:#cd5555"&gt;&amp;#34;{{ .spec.clusterIP }}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#00688b"&gt;SVC_REGISTRY&lt;/span&gt;=&lt;span style="color:#8b008b;font-weight:bold"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;oc get svc docker-registry -n default --template &lt;span style="color:#cd5555"&gt;&amp;#34;{{ .spec.clusterIP }}&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#8b008b;font-weight:bold"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get a token for your session&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>How to List Tags On Redhat Registry Images</title><link>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2016/07/11/List-Tags-On-Redhat-Registry-Images/</link><pubDate>Mon, 11 Jul 2016 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2016/07/11/List-Tags-On-Redhat-Registry-Images/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Ever gone to &lt;a href="https://access.redhat.com/search/#/container-images"&gt;RedHat&amp;rsquo;s container registry&lt;/a&gt; to search for an image and been left wondering what versions exist? Ever been frustrated by the inconsistent tag format? Is there a &lt;em&gt;v&lt;/em&gt; or is there not a &lt;em&gt;v&lt;/em&gt;? Me too.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Docker Hub has progressed to &lt;a href="https://docs.docker.com/registry/spec/api/"&gt;v2&lt;/a&gt;, while the RedHat registry is still &lt;a href="https://docs.docker.com/v1.6/reference/api/registry_api/"&gt;v1&lt;/a&gt; at the moment. As long as you use the right syntax, you can use curl to query the registry API and &lt;a href="https://docs.docker.com/v1.6/reference/api/registry_api/#list-repository-tags"&gt;list the tags&lt;/a&gt; like this:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Resources for Learning About Docker</title><link>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2015/04/19/Resources-for-Learning-Docker/</link><pubDate>Sun, 19 Apr 2015 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://guifreelife.com/blog/2015/04/19/Resources-for-Learning-Docker/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="tutorials"&gt;Tutorials&lt;/h1&gt;
